{
  "id": "Compound::DB00214 - Gene::1559",
  "verbalization": "Torasemide is likely to interact with Cyp2c9 through its binding to Cyp2c19, a cytochrome P450 enzyme involved in the metabolism of various substrates. The evidence suggests that Torasemide binds to Cyp2c19, which then participates in the activity of (r)- and (s)-limonene 6- and 7-monooxygenase, respectively. These enzymatic activities are ultimately participated by Cyp2c9, indicating a potential functional link between Torasemide and Cyp2c9. The overlapping roles of Cyp2c19 and Cyp2c9 in metabolizing limonene derivatives suggest that Torasemide may influence Cyp2c9's activity through a shared metabolic pathway. The consistent binding of Torasemide to Cyp2c19 across different paths supports the hypothesis that this interaction is central to the drug's effect on Cyp2c9.",
